  summary "Zhinghoua lang'Gleam discovers a discrepancy in the founding-era fire-core shipment records: fourteen cores were logged as delivered to the Promenade Ward's eastern quarter, but the heat-conductor array requires sixteen cores. Her investigation reveals that Summit-Lord Yahailong diverted two cores to build western perimeter heat-barriers against orca scouts, allowing two families—Moqai and Xuelin—to freeze during the founding's third winter. Yahailong then used Snowdrift-numb magic, taught to her by Hainou mewei'Frostglass, to alter the ice-memory and erase the families' names from the memorial. When Zhinghoua confronts Yahailong with evidence from the shadow-ledgers, Yahailong confesses that she chose to sacrifice two families to save the entire Ward, and has spent decades walking the conductor array in silent penance. Zhinghoua decides to bring the truth to council, accepting that the corrupted ice and the cost of revelation will reshape the colony's understanding of its own history."
